Table full name: NOAA_DATA_PLUS.NOAA_HURRICANES.HURRICANES
Column name: bom_tnum Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: iflag Type: TEXT Description: Interpolation Flag A 14 character flag string which denotes the source of each agency's report: Interpolation Flags include: _ == missing reports. No information provided. O == original report as provided by the agency. P == position was interpolated (all variables were interpolated/filled/nincluding intensity) I == Position was provided/nbut Intensity variables (and likely other variables) were interpolated/filled V = Position and intensity variables are original but some variables were interpolated/filled. The order of the 14 characters refers to the following 14 datasets: 1 - USA Agency (see column 18) 2 - Tokyo 3 - CMA 4 - HKO 5 - NewDelhi 6 - Reunion 7 - BoM 8 - Nadi 9 - Wellington 10 - ds824 11 - TD9636 12 - TD9635 13 - Neumann Southern Hemisphere data set 14 - M.L. Chenoweth N Atlantic Historic dataset
Column name: reunion_latitude Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: bom_r50_ne Type: NUMBER Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; storm-force (25m/s) or above. Northeast quadrant.
Column name: season Type: TEXT Description: 
Column name: ds824_pressure Type: NUMBER Description: 
Column name: hko_pressure Type: NUMBER Description: 
Column name: bom_eye Type: NUMBER Description: Mean radius of the cyclone eye.
Column name: nature Type: TEXT Description: Combined storm type. This is assigned based on all available storm types. They include: DS - Disturbance TS - Tropical ET - Extratropical SS - Subtropical NR - Not reported MX - Mixture (contradicting nature reports from different agencies)
Column name: reunion_longitude Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: usa_r50_sw Type: NUMBER Description: – 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: nadi_pressure Type: NUMBER Description: 
Column name: newdelhi_dp Type: NUMBER Description: 
Column name: bom_type Type: NUMBER Description: This indicates the type of system that this cyclone was at the time of the observation. Note that cyclones can evolve during their lifetimes and hence change type mid-stream (e.g. Extratropical transition (ETT))
Column name: bom_r64_nw Type: NUMBER Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; hurricane-force (33m/s) or above. Northwest quadrant
Column name: mlc_class Type: TEXT Description: Storm classification EX - Extratropical HU - Hurricane LO - Low MH SD - Subtropical depression SS - Subtropical storm TD - Tropical Depression TS - Tropical Storm TW WV - Open Wave
Column name: reunion_wind Type: NUMBER Description: Maximum average wind speed
Column name: reunion_r34_nw Type: NUMBER Description: 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: newdelhi_ci Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: usa_r50_ne Type: NUMBER Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: bom_r50_sw Type: NUMBER Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; storm-force (25m/s) or above. Southwest quadrant.
Column name: usa_r34_se Type: NUMBER Description: 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: bom_r64_se Type: NUMBER Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; hurricane-force (33m/s) or above. Southeast quadrant
Column name: reunion_r34_ne Type: NUMBER Description: 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r50_sw Type: NUMBER Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: mlc_wind Type: NUMBER Description: 
Column name: usa_r34_nw Type: NUMBER Description: – 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
